From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:11:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: apple: allow L1 PM substates on the J604's radio
 link

macOS runs the J604's radio link with all four L1 PM substates: the
ADT's /arm-io/apcie/pci-bridge0 carries pci-l1pm-control 0x4055190f,
which as an L1 PM Substates Control 1 word enables ASPM and PCI-PM L1.1
and L1.2. Both ends of the link advertise them, CLKREQ# is muxed for
the port and LTR is enabled, but on a devicetree platform the ASPM core
leaves the L1 substates out of a link's default, so the link only ever
goes to L1.

With radio_l1ss set, allow them on that link once the host has scanned
it: pci_enable_link_state() on the radio's function 0, L0s and L1 kept.
The ASPM core still enables only what both ends support and computes
the timings itself.

Off by default; only J604 machines act on it.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
index dec95de353..965880a88e 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/pcie-apple.c
@@ -5005,6 +5005,8 @@ static int apple_pcie_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	if (pcie->hw->tunneled)
 		pci_walk_bus(bridge->bus, apple_pcie_tunnel_keep_d0, NULL);
+	else if (READ_ONCE(radio_l1ss) && of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j604"))
+		apple_pcie_radio_l1ss(bridge);
 
 	return 0;
 }
